course: dictionary
lesson: 13584
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and inclination is one of them. The words around it tell you which meaning is right. «I had no inclination to go out in the rain» means I did not want to go out, because of the words wanting and go out.
explain: In maths and science, inclination means a slope or slant. «The inclination of the ramp made the ball roll faster.» Here the clues are ramp and roll: a steeper slope makes the ball go faster. The Earth's axis also has an inclination, which is its tilt.
explain: Inclination can also mean a natural tendency, as in «She has a strong inclination to help others.» It can mean a small bow or nod of the head too, as in «The butler gave a small inclination of his head.» Swap each meaning into the sentence and see which one fits.
fact: Inclination means a feeling of wanting to do something, or a liking for something.
fact: In maths and science, inclination means a slope, a slant, or the angle of a slope.
fact: «Inclination» can also mean a natural tendency to behave in a certain way, or a small bow or nod of the head.
fact: «Have no inclination» means you do not want to do something, and «by inclination» means by nature or by what you naturally prefer.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «The inclination of the ramp made the ball roll faster.» What does inclination mean here? | *A slope or slant | A small bow | A loud noise | A feeling of wanting to play
exercise: «I had no inclination to go out in the rain.» What does inclination mean here? | A steep hill | A nod of the head | A kind of rain | *A wish or feeling of wanting to do something
exercise: «The butler gave a small inclination of his head.» What does inclination mean here? | *A small bow or nod | A slope | A tilt of the Earth | A tendency to be clumsy
test: «The Earth's axis has an inclination, which is its tilt.» In science, what does inclination mean? | Sleepiness | A nod of the head | Happiness | *Angle or tilt
test: «She has a strong inclination to help others.» What does inclination mean here? | Sleepiness | A small bow | A slope | *A natural tendency to behave in a certain way
exam: «Sam reads quietly, by inclination.» What does "by inclination" suggest? | By accident | *Because he naturally prefers it | After a long walk | Because a teacher made him
